     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum for immediate-release metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day. The maximum is usually given as 850 mg three times daily, or 1,000 mg twice daily. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day). This is the most likely intended dose, since 1700 may be a transcription error.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg PO** at a different frequency.\n- **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that it's intentional and give the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy before it's entered."
      }
     ],
